---

<!-- Choice Board Container -->
<div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 20px; width: 95%; margin: 20px auto;">

  <!-- Card 1 -->
  <details style="background-color: #0093A4; color: #FFFFFF; padding: 20px; border-radius: 20px; box-shadow: 4px 4px 10px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);">
    <summary style="font-size: 16pt; font-weight: bold; cursor: pointer;">
      Understand the Problem
    </summary>
    <p style="font-size: 12pt; margin-top: 12px;">
      Read the problem carefully. Identify what is being asked and what information is given.
    </p>
    <p style="font-size: 12pt;">
      Ask yourself: What do I already know? What is unclear?
    </p>
  </details>

  <!-- Card 2 -->
  <details style="background-color: #8C52BA; color: #FFFFFF; padding: 20px; border-radius: 20px; box-shadow: 4px 4px 10px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);">
    <summary style="font-size: 16pt; font-weight: bold; cursor: pointer;">
      Make a Plan
    </summary>
    <p style="font-size: 12pt; margin-top: 12px;">
      Decide on steps you can follow to solve the problem.
    </p>
    <p style="font-size: 12pt;">
      You might draw a diagram, write pseudocode, or list steps in order.
    </p>
  </details>

  <!-- Card 3 -->
  <details style="background-color: #292F36; color: #FFFFFF; padding: 20px; border-radius: 20px; box-shadow: 4px 4px 10px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);">
    <summary style="font-size: 16pt; font-weight: bold; cursor: pointer;">
      Try It
    </summary>
    <p style="font-size: 12pt; margin-top: 12px;">
      Follow your plan and start building your solution.
    </p>
    <p style="font-size: 12pt;">
      It’s okay if it doesn’t work the first time.
    </p>
  </details>

  <!-- Card 4 -->
  <details style="background-color: #F7F8FA; color: #000000; padding: 20px; border-radius: 20px; box-shadow: 4px 4px 10px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);">
    <summary style="font-size: 16pt; font-weight: bold; cursor: pointer;">
      Debug
    </summary>
    <p style="font-size: 12pt; margin-top: 12px;">
      Look for errors or unexpected behavior.
    </p>
    <p style="font-size: 12pt;">
      Change one thing at a time and test again.
    </p>
  </details>

  <!-- Card 5 -->
  <details style="background-color: #DECEEA; color: #000000; padding: 20px; border-radius: 20px; box-shadow: 4px 4px 10px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);">
    <summary style="font-size: 16pt; font-weight: bold; cursor: pointer;">
      Reflect
    </summary>
    <p style="font-size: 12pt; margin-top: 12px;">
      Think about what worked well and what was challenging.
    </p>
    <p style="font-size: 12pt;">
      How might you solve a similar problem next time?
    </p>
  </details>

  <!-- Card 6 -->
  <details style="background-color: #B7E0E5; color: #000000; padding: 20px; border-radius: 20px; box-shadow: 4px 4px 10px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);">
    <summary style="font-size: 16pt; font-weight: bold; cursor: pointer;">
      Share Your Thinking
    </summary>
    <p style="font-size: 12pt; margin-top: 12px;">
      Explain your solution to a partner or group.
    </p>
    <p style="font-size: 12pt;">
      Focus on your process, not just the final answer.
    </p>
  </details>

</div>

<!-- Game Container -->
<div style="background-color: #F7F8FA; padding: 20px; border-radius: 20px; width: 95%; margin: 20px auto; box-shadow: 4px 4px 12px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);">

  <p style="font-size: 14pt; font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 10px;">🕵️‍♀️ Choose the statement you think is the lie:</p>

  <ol style="font-size: 12pt; line-height: 1.6;">
    <li><strong>Planning</strong> is an important step that helps you organize your thoughts before starting.</li>
    <li><strong>Debugging</strong> only happens after the project is completely finished.</li>
    <li><strong>Reflection</strong> helps you think about what worked and what didn’t.</li>
  </ol>

  <details style="margin-top: 20px; background-color: #0093A4; color: #FFFFFF; padding: 15px; border-radius: 15px; cursor: pointer;">
    <summary style="font-size: 14pt; font-weight: bold;">🎉 Reveal the Answer</summary>
    <p style="font-size: 12pt; margin-top: 12px;">
      ❌ <strong>Statement #2 is the lie!</strong><br>
      Debugging can (and should!) happen throughout the process—not just at the end. It's how you spot mistakes and improve your solution as you go. ✅
    </p>
  </details>

</div>

<!-- 3-Column Game Layout -->
<div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 20px; width: 95%; margin: 20px auto;">

  <!-- Column 1: Problem Solving Process -->
  <div style="background-color: #F7F8FA; padding: 20px; border-radius: 20px; box-shadow: 4px 4px 10px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);">
    <p style="font-size: 14pt; font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 10px;">🧠 Problem Solving</p>
    <ol style="font-size: 12pt; line-height: 1.6; padding-left: 20px;">
      <li>Planning helps organize your thoughts before coding.</li>
      <li>Debugging only happens after everything is built.</li>
      <li>Reflection helps you learn from what you built.</li>
    </ol>
    <details style="margin-top: 15px; background-color: #0093A4; color: #FFFFFF; padding: 10px; border-radius: 12px;">
      <summary style="font-size: 13pt; font-weight: bold;">🎉 Reveal Answer</summary>
      <p style="font-size: 12pt; margin-top: 10px;">
        ❌ <strong>Statement #2 is the lie!</strong><br>
        Debugging happens throughout the process, not just at the end. ✅
      </p>
    </details>
  </div>

  <!-- Column 2: Computational Thinking -->
  <div style="background-color: #DECEEA; padding: 20px; border-radius: 20px; box-shadow: 4px 4px 10px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);">
    <p style="font-size: 14pt; font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 10px;">🤖 Computational Thinking</p>
    <ol style="font-size: 12pt; line-height: 1.6; padding-left: 20px;">
      <li>Decomposition means combining all the small steps at once.</li>
      <li>Algorithms are step-by-step instructions for solving problems.</li>
      <li>Pattern recognition helps find similarities in problems.</li>
    </ol>
    <details style="margin-top: 15px; background-color: #8C52BA; color: #FFFFFF; padding: 10px; border-radius: 12px;">
      <summary style="font-size: 13pt; font-weight: bold;">🎉 Reveal Answer</summary>
      <p style="font-size: 12pt; margin-top: 10px;">
        ❌ <strong>Statement #1 is the lie!</strong><br>
        Decomposition means breaking a big problem into smaller parts, not combining them. 🧩
      </p>
    </details>
  </div>

  <!-- Column 3: Debugging & Teamwork -->
  <div style="background-color: #B7E0E5; padding: 20px; border-radius: 20px; box-shadow: 4px 4px 10px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);">
    <p style="font-size: 14pt; font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 10px;">🛠️ Debugging & Teamwork</p>
    <ol style="font-size: 12pt; line-height: 1.6; padding-left: 20px;">
      <li>It’s okay to ask a partner for help while debugging.</li>
      <li>Teamwork slows down the problem solving process.</li>
      <li>Explaining your thinking can help you find bugs.</li>
    </ol>
    <details style="margin-top: 15px; background-color: #292F36; color: #FFFFFF; padding: 10px; border-radius: 12px;">
      <summary style="font-size: 13pt; font-weight: bold;">🎉 Reveal Answer</summary>
      <p style="font-size: 12pt; margin-top: 10px;">
        ❌ <strong>Statement #2 is the lie!</strong><br>
        Teamwork actually helps you solve problems more effectively—not slower. 🤝
      </p>
    </details>
  </div>

</div>

<!-- 3-Column Game Layout with Improved Readability -->
<div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 20px; width: 95%; margin: 20px auto;">

  <!-- Column 1: Problem Solving -->
  <div style="background-color: #F7F8FA; padding: 20px; border-radius: 20px; box-shadow: 4px 4px 10px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);">
    <p style="font-size: 14pt; font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 10px;">🧠 Problem Solving</p>
    <ol style="font-size: 12pt; line-height: 1.8; padding-left: 20px; margin-bottom: 20px;">
      <li><strong>Planning</strong> helps organize your thoughts before coding.</li>
      <li><strong>Debugging</strong> only happens after everything is built.</li>
      <li><strong>Reflection</strong> helps you learn from what you built.</li>
    </ol>
    <details style="background-color: #0093A4; color: #FFFFFF; padding: 10px; border-radius: 12px;">
      <summary style="font-size: 13pt; font-weight: bold;">🎉 Reveal Answer</summary>
      <p style="font-size: 12pt; margin-top: 10px;">
        ❌ <strong>Statement #2 is the lie!</strong><br>
        Debugging happens throughout the process, not just at the end. ✅
      </p>
    </details>
  </div>

  <!-- Column 2: Computational Thinking -->
  <div style="background-color: #DECEEA; padding: 20px; border-radius: 20px; box-shadow: 4px 4px 10px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);">
    <p style="font-size: 14pt; font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 10px;">🤖 Computational Thinking</p>
    <ol style="font-size: 12pt; line-height: 1.8; padding-left: 20px; margin-bottom: 20px;">
      <li><strong>Decomposition</strong> means combining all the small steps at once.</li>
      <li><strong>Algorithms</strong> are step-by-step instructions for solving problems.</li>
      <li><strong>Pattern recognition</strong> helps find similarities in problems.</li>
    </ol>
    <details style="background-color: #8C52BA; color: #FFFFFF; padding: 10px; border-radius: 12px;">
      <summary style="font-size: 13pt; font-weight: bold;">🎉 Reveal Answer</summary>
      <p style="font-size: 12pt; margin-top: 10px;">
        ❌ <strong>Statement #1 is the lie!</strong><br>
        Decomposition means breaking a big problem into smaller parts, not combining them. 🧩
      </p>
    </details>
  </div>




  <!-- Column 3: Debugging & Teamwork -->
  <div style="background-color: #B7E0E5; padding: 20px; border-radius: 20px; box-shadow: 4px 4px 10px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);">
    <p style="font-size: 14pt; font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 10px;">🛠️ Debugging & Teamwork</p>
    <ol style="font-size: 12pt; line-height: 1.8; padding-left: 20px; margin-bottom: 20px;">
      <li>It’s okay to <strong>ask a partner</strong> for help while debugging.</li>
      <li><strong>Teamwork</strong> slows down the problem solving process.</li>
      <li><strong>Explaining your thinking</strong> can help you find bugs.</li>
    </ol>
    <details style="background-color: #292F36; color: #FFFFFF; padding: 10px; border-radius: 12px;">
      <summary style="font-size: 13pt; font-weight: bold;">🎉 Reveal Answer</summary>
      <p style="font-size: 12pt; margin-top: 10px;">
        ❌ <strong>Statement #2 is the lie!</strong><br>
        Teamwork actually helps you solve problems more effectively—not slower. 
      </p>
    </details>
  </div>

</div>
